
# 🪨📄✂️ Rock Paper Scissors – Python Winter Sprint 2026

A Python-based **Rock–Paper–Scissors (RPS) Engine** built as part of the **Python Winter Sprint 2026** by **Coding Council**.  
This project focuses on strengthening Python fundamentals through **conditionals, loops, and Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)**.

---

## 🎯 Objective

Build a command-line Rock–Paper–Scissors game where:
- The user selects a move
- The computer selects a move
- The winner is decided using game rules
- Scores are tracked across rounds

---

## 🧠 Tracks Overview

### 🔰 Foundation Track (Beginners)
**Core Topic:** Conditional Expressions  
- User inputs a move (`rock`, `paper`, `scissors`)
- Computer move is predefined or random
- Result is decided using `if / elif / else`

---

### ⚙️ Core Track (OOP Based)
**Core Topic:** Object-Oriented Programming  

Features:
- `RPSGame` class
- Player name & score tracking
- Multiple rounds
- Final score display

---

### 🚀 Project Track (Advanced – Mini Project)
A complete **CLI-based RPS Engine** with:

- User authentication (login/register)
- Persistent user profiles
- Match-based gameplay
- File-backed storage (`users.json`)
- Modular OOP design

---

## 🧩 Project Features

- ✅ Register & Login system
- 🎮 Rock–Paper–Scissors game engine
- 📊 Persistent player statistics
- 🔁 Multi-round matches
- 💾 File-based data storage
- 🧱 Clean OOP architecture

---

## 🏗️ Class Design

### 👤 `User` Class
Handles:
- Username & password
- Wins, losses, draws
- Loading & saving user data

---

### 🎮 `RPSEngine` Class
Handles:
- Valid moves
- Computer move generation
- Rule-based result calculation

---

### 🔁 `GameSession` Class
Handles:
- Number of rounds
- Match flow
- Score tracking
- Updating user statistics

---

